# Change: Em-D and Em-G (repertoire plan: st-change-em-d-em-g). An original chord-change study.
# Each half is a ladder that changes faster and faster: the home chord Em held for two bars (one
# strum a bar), then a change every bar with two strums, every bar with four strums, and every
# two beats. First half: Em (022000) with D (xx0232: finger 1 on string 3 fret 2, 3 on string 2
# fret 3, 2 on string 1 fret 2; strum strings 4 to 1 only). Second half: Em with G (320003).
# Em is fingered 1 and 2 (1 on string 5, 2 on string 4) and G 2-1-3 (2 on string 6 fret 3,
# 1 on string 5 fret 2, 3 on string 1 fret 3), so finger 1 never leaves string 5, fret 2.
# Keep the metronome on: the new chord lands on the beat even if the strum before it catches
# open strings. The teacher plays an original tune whose notes on beats 1 and 3 belong to the
# chord in force (E minor, without C or C#).
title: Change: Em-D and Em-G
id: st-change-em-d-em-g
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original chord-change study for Sixstring Academy
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 2
tags: chord changes, strumming, metronome, anchor finger, em, d, g
tempo: 60
time: 4/4
key: Em

track: Your strum
role: rhythm
[Em and D]
| ^"One strum a bar" "Em=022000" w D | D | ^"Two strums a bar" "D=xx0232" h D D | "Em=022000" D D |
| ^"Four strums a bar" "D=xx0232" q D D D D | "Em=022000" D D D D | ^"Change every two beats" "D=xx0232" D D "Em=022000" D D | "D=xx0232" D D "Em=022000" D D ||
[Em and G]
| ^"Finger 1 stays on string 5, fret 2" "Em=022000" w D | D | ^"Two strums a bar" "G=320003" h D D | "Em=022000" D D |
| ^"Four strums a bar" "G=320003" q D D D D | "Em=022000" D D D D | ^"Change every two beats" "G=320003" D D "Em=022000" D D | "G=320003" D D "Em=022000" h D ||

track: Teacher
role: lead
[Em and D]
